// Canonical Go resilience module requirements (#1144).
//
// A go.mod FRAGMENT, not a module file: fold this require line into the same
// go.mod you folded the ops-api payload's into, then `go mod tidy`. Place
// dependency_catalog.go and dependency_health.go into the repo FIRST -- tidy
// removes any requirement no package in the working tree imports, so run against a
// tree that does not yet contain them and it silently strips this line and exits 0.
//
// ONE library, deliberately. gobreaker is the blessed Go circuit breaker; the
// bounded jittered retry is ~30 lines of stdlib inside dependency_catalog.go
// rather than a second dependency. See README.md, "Why gobreaker and no retry
// library" -- the short version is that the retry has to be breaker-aware anyway
// (never retry an open breaker's rejection), so a library would be wrapped in that
// predicate regardless, and every bootstrapped repo would carry a second version
// surface for it.
//
// The version is a floor, not a pin -- Renovate/Dependabot move it. Note the /v2
// import path: gobreaker v2 made the breaker generic (CircuitBreaker[T]), and the
// payload stores CircuitBreaker[any] so one catalog can hold breakers for
// dependencies whose calls return different types.

require github.com/sony/gobreaker/v2 v2.4.0
